IPW makefile boilerplate.

Files:
	local	macros that will probably have to be redefined for different
		UNIX environments

		Preconfigured versions of this file for various existing IPW
		hosts may be found in the subdirectory "conf".  See the README
		file therein.

	std	(hopefully) portable macros

	debug	overrides certain std macros, used by ipwmake -D

	profile	overrides certain std macros, used by ipwmake -P

	rules	actual rules used by "make"

		NOTE: This file WILL need to be edited if the AR_XOPTS defined
		      in "local" does NOT cause "ar" to restore the original
		      modification times of the extracted files.  See the
		      comments in the "lib" target.

		      Be warned that this kludge will cause all the ".o" files
		      associated with library sources to be left in the source
		      directories, as well as in the library archives, and
		      will thus cause some additional disk space to be
		      consumed.  Presumably, this is preferable to having to
		      recompile the whole library every time you change
		      something.

Concatenation order:
	local
	std
	[debug OR profile]
	{Makedefs}
	rules

Standard macro suffixes:
	suffix		contents
	--------	---------------------------------------------------
	_LOCAL		localisms, machine dependencies, etc.  Always used.
	_NORMAL		used if no -D or -P argument to ipwmake
	_DEBUG		used if ipwmake -D
	_PROFILE	used if ipwmake -P
	_PREFIX		prepended to a filename
	_SUFFIX		appended to a filename
	_STD		always used, including relevant _LOCAL
	_OPTION		one of relevant _NORMAL, _DEBUG, or _PROFILE
	_DIR		directory
	_MODE		protection mode

